The `fs_try_exists` failure is pre-existing on the untouched baseline (container environment issue), unrelated to this fix. All sync/mpsc tests pass.

## Summary

**Root cause** (tokio/src/sync/mpsc/block.rs:182): `Block::has_value(slot_index)` blindly masked the slot index into the block via `offset()` (`index & (BLOCK_CAP - 1)`). After the receiver consumed the last slot of a block, `rx.index` points into the *next* block, but `rx.head` only advances during `pop()`. When `is_empty()` was then called, `list_head_has_value` checked the stale head block with a wrapped-around index — matching slot 0's ready bit (still set from the consumed value) and incorrectly reporting a value present, even though `len() == 0`. This happened exactly at every 32-message (`BLOCK_CAP`) boundary.

**Fix**: applied the upstream fix — `has_value` now returns `false` when the given index falls outside `start_index .. start_index + BLOCK_CAP`, so it never confuses indices from a different block:

```rust
pub(crate) fn has_value(&self, slot_index: usize) -> bool {
    if slot_index < self.header.start_index {
        return false;
    }
    if slot_index >= self.header.start_index + BLOCK_CAP {
